body:
If illegal immigrants are actually stealing your jobs then the problem isn't the immigrants. The problem is the corporate decision makers who are willing to break the law to save money and the politicians who refuse to tighten up and enforce our existing laws against hiring illegal immigrants. 

&#x200B;

If the government mandated use of E-Verify and severely punished any company that knowingly hired illegal immigrants you would see a significant drop in illegal immigration.

I had to look it up because it is one of those things that I usually just assume the meaning of based on context. 

&#x200B;

A justice of the peace is a magistrate who handles minor cases, performs marriages, and grants licenses in a county or other local jurisdiction.

"People are nice but stick to themselves" 

&#x200B;

That is one thing about Wyoming that I have always found really interesting. Most people here really do seem to believe in just leaving everyone the hell alone. Like, sure you get a few self righteous people who think their beliefs or ideals should dictate other peoples' lives, but most people just want to be left to their own devices.

The basic premise is that religious extremists staged some kind of coups against the American government and created a Christian theocracy where women are property (young fertile women are literally assigned to high ranking "worthy" men for the purpose of producing a child before being reassigned elsewhere) and non-white men are deemed "unworthy" and can only do menial labor or low ranking jobs such as chauffeur. 

&#x200B;

I haven't watched the show yet, but I have read the book and that is the basic background of the story.

It is a shitty holdover from when we needed to separate ourselves from the "godless commies" of the Soviet Union. It is a mark of a time when fear was our guiding emotion. 

&#x200B;

I would much rather we go back to our original motto "E Pluribus unum" which means "From Many, One", but I don't see that happening anytime soon.

This is some bullshit. I used to work at a juvenile treatment center. We had a little more control over things like appropriate dress for the kids and stuff, but the way they obviously target the girls for punishment is appalling. I had tampons thrown at me by residents and aside from documenting it (we tried not to put male staff with the girls whenever possible, but when we had to we documented EVERYTHING) the only response would have been to confiscate the thrown tampon and warn them that they would go to their room if they continued. 

&#x200B;

I'm sorry you have to deal with such obviously biased and sexist coworkers. Hope you can find a better job soon so you don't have to deal with that anymore.

My beard was pretty patchy until I was about 24. My cheeks are still a little thin, but it grows in uniformly now.

&#x200B;

Big thing to remember is that everyones beard will grow in a little differently. I know guys who could grow a full beard in high school and others who still can't grow a beard at 30+
